 ## Background
-The scaled Bernstein form was proposed in [SR03] (cited in [S1, unofficial]) as an alternative to the power form for polynomial evaluation in rendering. It is particularly useful in volume rendering where trivariate polynomials are composed with ray parameterizations. The method was highlighted in [S1, unofficial] for its ability to reduce register usage and improve parallelism on GPUs by fitting the computation into limited register space.
